            <ArticleTitle>PGD for the m.14487 T&gt;C mitochondrial DNA mutation resulted in the birth of a healthy boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>698-703</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/humrep/dew356</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the first PGD performed for the m.14487 T&gt;C mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA) mutation in the MT-ND6 gene, associated with Leigh syndrome. The female carrier gave birth to a healthy baby boy at age 42. This case adds to the successes of PGD for mtDNA mutations.</AbstractText>
